Part B: Internetwork Using a Wireless Router, DHCP Server, and Internet Cloud
Algorithm / Procedure
1. Place an Internet cloud, wireless router, two laptops, and a server or PC in the workspace.
2. Connect the Internet cloud or ISP-facing device to the wireless router's Internet/WAN port, where supported.
3. Open the wireless router configuration.
4. Configure the wireless SSID and security settings.
5. Enable the DHCP server and specify an appropriate address range.
6. Connect the laptops to the wireless network using the configured SSID and password.
7. Configure the server or PC as required.
8. Verify that wireless clients receive IP addresses automatically.
9. Test connectivity to the local server or gateway using ping.
10. If an ISP-side network is configured, test connectivity to a reachable device on that network.
