Part C: Internetwork Using Switches, Router, and Ethernet Cables
Algorithm / Procedure
1. Place two switches, one router, and four PCs in Cisco Packet Tracer.
2. Connect two PCs to each switch.
3. Connect each switch to a different router interface using Ethernet cables.
4. Assign static IP addresses to the PCs and router interfaces.
5. Configure the router interfaces using the CLI and enable them.
6. Verify the interface status using show ip interface brief.
7. Send ping requests between PCs connected to different switches.
8. Observe packet forwarding in Simulation mode.

Observation
- Switches forward frames within their local LANs.
- Routers connect different IP networks.
- Ethernet cables provide wired connectivity between PCs, switches, and router interfaces.
- Simulation mode shows the path followed by packets across the internetwork.

Result
An internetwork was designed and configured in Cisco Packet Tracer using routers, switches, and Ethernet cables. Static IP addressing and router interface configuration were performed, packet transmission between different networks was simulated, and a wireless router with DHCP was configured to demonstrate automatic IP address allocation.
